course: dictionary
lesson: 5900
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A marathon is about 42 km, so a 2 km school cross-country is about 21 times shorter.» Here the words about kilometres show that a marathon is a long running race.
explain: «We watched a marathon of cartoons all Saturday.» There are no running shoes here. Ask: what would fit? Try swapping in "a very long event" and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so marathon means any very long activity.
explain: Marathon can also be an adjective, a describing word. In «a marathon meeting», it tells you what kind of meeting it was: a very long one. Adjectives come before the noun they describe, so look for the word it is next to.
fact: A marathon is a running race of about 42 kilometres (26.2 miles).
fact: A half marathon is half that distance.
fact: «Marathon» can also mean any very long activity, such as «a homework marathon».
fact: «Marathon» is also a place name, linked to a famous battle in 490 BC, when the Athenians beat a Persian army there.
fact: The story of a runner racing to Athens with the news is a legend told much later, not a record of what happened.
exercise: «A marathon is about 42 km, so a 2 km school cross-country is about 21 times shorter.» What is a marathon? | *A running race of about 42 kilometres | A quick sprint across a classroom | A short walk around the school field | A game played with a ball and two teams
exercise: «We watched a marathon of cartoons all Saturday.» What does marathon mean here? | A fast film | *Any very long event | A kind of cartoon character | A running race of 42 kilometres
exercise: In «a marathon meeting», what job does marathon do? | *It describes the meeting and means very long | It is the name of a place | It is a type of shoe | It names a running race
test: What is a half marathon about? | About 84 kilometres | *About 21 kilometres | About 42 metres | About 4 kilometres
test: Which sentence uses marathon to mean a very long activity? | «He bought new marathon trainers.» | «She ran a marathon through the city centre.» | «The marathon started at nine o'clock.» | *«We had a marathon game of chess that lasted all afternoon.»
exam: In «a marathon session», what does marathon mean? | A running race of 42 kilometres | *Very long, lasting a long time | A kind of sport shoe | A short break from work
